  "provenance": {
    "source_notes": "Modeled on a fan-made novelty-plate graphic the Forza Writer user supplied, itself inspired by Night City vehicle plates in Cyberpunk 2077 -- not a screenshot of the game itself or an extracted/official CD Projekt Red asset. Layout: a dark diagonal block along the left edge, bold 'NC 77' text (read as Night City / the game's 2077 setting), a small flag-like emblem in the top-right corner, and a dark lower band containing a glitch/barcode-style pattern of vertical bars. The left block's jagged torn edge and the emblem's specific graphic (a star over banded colors, whose in-universe meaning isn't identifiable from the image alone) are both simplified to plain rectangles here -- the schema has no torn-edge or icon/star decoration primitive. The bar pattern reuses the same repeated-'|' approximation as the Halo: Reach barcode template above, through the ordinary fontpack pipeline rather than a dedicated barcode renderer.",
